  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "If \\(x=(\\log_8 2)^{(\\log_2 8)},\\) then \\(\\log_3 x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-3\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac13\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac13\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A logarithm asks which exponent produces the stated number. Since \\(8^{1/3}=2\\) and \\(2^3=8\\),\n\\[\n\\log_8 2=\\frac13,\n\\qquad\n\\log_2 8=3.\n\\]\nSubstituting these values gives\n\\[\nx=\\left(\\frac13\\right)^3\n=\\frac1{27}=3^{-3}.\n\\]\nThis value of \\(x\\) is positive, so its logarithm is defined. Because \\(3^{-3}=x\\), we obtain \\(\\log_3 x=\\boxed{-3}\\), choice A.",
